* @title Table-to-array conversion and data type inspection
* @attribution Griswold 1971, Chapter 7
* @expect >>>
* PROTOTYPE: 2,2
* TYPE OF A<1,1>: STRING
* TYPE OF A<1,2>: INTEGER
* <<<
         T = TABLE(5)
         T<'RED'> = 1
         T<'BLUE'> = 2
         A = CONVERT(T, 'ARRAY')
         OUTPUT = 'PROTOTYPE: ' PROTOTYPE(A)
         OUTPUT = 'TYPE OF A<1,1>: ' DATATYPE(A<1,1>)
         OUTPUT = 'TYPE OF A<1,2>: ' DATATYPE(A<1,2>)
END
